    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a pretty strong claim to call it the \"gold standard.\" But doesn't that approach ignore how different cultures prioritize collective stability over individual expression? Some would argue that the US model actually causes social fragmentation and instability, which is why many other nations feel they have no choice but to regulate more strictly. Can you explain why the US approach is objectively better than a model that prioritizes social cohesion?",
