      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The US model is not a one-size-fits-all solution, but it's the only way to preserve the very fabric of a free society. Prioritizing social cohesion over individual expression can lead to a slippery slope where dissenting voices are silenced, and the government becomes increasingly authoritarian. The US approach may not be perfect, but it's the only way to ensure that the rights of the minority are protected, and that the government doesn't become a tool for the majority to suppress dissent.",
